@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Native repair plan
+
+## Modification History
+
+| Date | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| 2026-11-02 | Implemented the approved P2 native startup coordination correction. |
+
+Evidence -> {native correction + CPU communication checks, package preparation in Frontier} -> independent review -> source freeze -> Frontier package freeze -> formal generation 02.
+
+Online nonelastic MoE DP rank0's CoreEngineProcManager owns a TCPStore that binds port 0 before startup. HELLO sends its actual port. Engine groups retain the bound-socket path, use distinct sequence keys, and select the legacy TCPStore backend needed to adopt master_listen_fd. Workers initialize their existing default process group through a dp_worker_world PrefixStore on the same coordination listener. This avoids reusing the unreserved port list for workers. The engine sequence is hash-excluded. Elastic keys and offline paths retain their prior behavior.
+
+Acceptance: two and four ranks with free/occupied preselected ports communicate; two consecutive engine groups have distinct ports; two worker shards per DP rank communicate; simultaneous independent role groups succeed; listener released on shutdown; source review and immutable package binding. Full GPU runtime is verified only by the parent task's formal run.
