+# Native DP startup repair archive
+
+## Modification History
+
+| Date | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| 2026-11-02 | Archived the source/CPU deliverable; full GPU validation belongs to the parent Frontier task. |
+
+Four startup files now coordinate online nonelastic MoE DP initialization through a launcher-owned TCPStore. Engine groups publish reserved listeners under sequence keys; worker-world rendezvous uses an independent PrefixStore. Tensor/data/expert geometry, model execution and serving timing code are unchanged.
+
+Local CPU validation used Python3.12.13, torch2.8.0+cu128: six role cases, 16 engine ranks, 32 engine group initializations and 32 worker ranks completed actual all-reduce. Free and occupied old-port cases passed for DP2 and DP4; simultaneous P/D and listener release passed. The native functions are extracted verbatim; configuration/model body/NUMA/world wrapper are fixtures. This is not a full native GPU test.
+
+Independent Pi review p64-native-review-1102h found no actionable source defect in the current nnodes=1/nonelastic/MP/MoE path. The parent task retains the CPU runner, commands, results, review and complete patch, freezes the package, and owns pinned-image CPU plus formal P2-64 validation.
